>> title: Cà Phê Sữa Đá
>> category: Drinks
>> tags: coffee, vietnamese, condensed milk, iced, drink
>> counters: Phở & Bánh Mì
>> aka: ca phe sua da, cà phê sữa đá, Vietnamese iced coffee, Vietnamese coffee, iced coffee with condensed milk, cafe sua da, cà phê đá, ca phe da, phin coffee, D1
>> pairs-with: banh-mi-dac-biet
>> servings: 1
>> time: 10 min
>> step.1: spoon the milk, set the phin on top
>> step.2: load and level the grounds
>> step.3: bloom 30 sec
>> step.4: fill and let it drip 4 min
>> step.5: stir, then pour over ice

Spoon @sweetened condensed milk{3%Tbs}(45 mL) into the bottom of a heatproof #glass{} and set a #phin filter{} on the rim.

Tip @Vietnamese dark roast coffee{3%Tbs}(20 g; coarse, chicory in it if you can get it) into @&(~1)filter and glass{}, tap it level, and screw the press plate down finger-tight — no harder, or nothing comes through.

Wet @&(~1)grounds{} with @boiling water{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and ~bloom{30%sec}, until the bed swells up against the plate.

Fill @&(~1)phin{} with @boiling water{1/2%cup}(120 mL), cap it, and ~steep{4%min} while it drips. Four minutes is right; under two means the grind is too coarse and over six means it is too fine, and both are fixed at the grinder rather than at the press.

Stir @&(~1)coffee and milk{} until the milk lifts off the bottom and the whole glass goes the colour of caramel, then pour it over @ice{2%cup} in a tall #glass{}.
